.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt PAZARI-AGENT.TOML 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pazari-agent.toml
.Nd configuration file for pazari-agent
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr pazari-agent 1
reads its configuration from a TOML file,
.Pa /etc/pazari/agent.toml
by default.
.Ql pazari-agent example-config
prints a complete file with every key at its default.
.Pp
How the agent uses these settings is described in
.Xr pazari-agent 1 .
.Ss Sizes, durations and counts
A
.Ar size
is an integer number of bytes, or a number followed by a unit.
.Cm KiB , MiB , GiB
and
.Cm TiB
are powers of 1024;
.Cm kB , MB , GB
and
.Cm TB
are powers of 1000.
Units are case-insensitive and may be preceded by a space.
.Pp
A
.Ar duration
is a string such as
.Ql 500ms ,
.Ql 5s ,
.Ql 1min
or
.Ql "2s 500ms" .
Units range from
.Cm ns
to
.Cm y .
Unless stated otherwise, a duration must be greater than zero and at most 24
hours.
.Pp
A
.Ar count
is an integer greater than zero.
.Sh SETTINGS
.Ss [tick]\&
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm interval No = Ar duration
How often the agent samples the workload cgroup and the guest's memory.
Default
.Cm 1s .
.El
.Ss [workload]\&
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm cgroup No = Ar path
Absolute path of the workload cgroup, for example
.Pa /sys/fs/cgroup/workload.slice .
Required.
.It Cm service_reserve No = Ar size
Memory kept below
.Va memory.max
for everything in the guest other than the workload.
Required; may be 0.
.It Cm burst_reserve No = Ar size
The gap between
.Va memory.high
and
.Va memory.max .
Required; must be greater than 0.
See
.Sx SIZING .
.El
.Ss [workload.backend]\&
How the agent sets
.Va memory.high
and
.Va memory.max .
Other cgroup files are always written directly.
Optional; defaults to
.Cm cgroupfs .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm cgroupfs
Write the cgroup files directly.
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm systemd
Set
.Va MemoryHigh
and
.Va MemoryMax
as runtime properties of a unit over D-Bus.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm unit No = Ar name
The unit, for example
.Ql workload.slice .
Required.
.El
.El
.Ss [host]\&
The session with
.Xr pazarid 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm handshake_timeout No = Ar duration
How long to wait for the daemon to answer a new connection.
Default
.Cm 10s .
.It Cm reconnect_min No = Ar duration
First reconnect delay.
Default
.Cm 500ms .
.It Cm reconnect_max No = Ar duration
Maximum reconnect delay; the delay doubles up to this.
Must be at least
.Cm reconnect_min .
Default
.Cm 30s .
.El
.Ss [host.transport]\&
How the agent reaches
.Xr pazarid 1 .
Required.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm vsock
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm cid No = Ar integer
The host's context ID.
Default
.Cm 2 .
.It Cm port No = Ar integer
Default
.Cm 4650 .
.El
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm unix
For guests that are not virtual machines.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm path No = Ar path
The daemon's socket.
Required.
.El
.El
.Ss [resize]\&
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm settle_grace No = Ar duration
How long to wait for granted memory to arrive before accepting the size the
guest has.
Default
.Cm 10s .
.It Cm deny_backoff No = Ar duration
How long to wait before retrying a refused request, when the host does not
specify a delay.
Default
.Cm 5s .
.It Cm hotplug_debounce No = Ar duration
After a memory hot-plug event, how long to wait for further events before
re-reading the guest's memory.
Default
.Cm 250ms .
.El
.Ss [reclaim]\&
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm chunk No = Ar size
The largest single
.Va memory.reclaim
write.
Default
.Cm 64MiB .
.It Cm swappiness No = Ar integer
The
.Va swappiness
passed to each
.Va memory.reclaim
write, from 0 to 200.
If unset, the guest's
.Va vm.swappiness
applies.
.El
.Ss [throttle]\&
What the agent does when the workload throttles at
.Va memory.high .
Optional; defaults to
.Cm grow .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm grow
Ask the host for more at once.
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm reclaim
Reclaim from the workload cgroup before asking the host.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm amount No = Ar size
How much one reclaim asks for.
The agent asks the host at once when the guest has less than this to spare.
Default
.Cm 256MiB .
.El
.El
.Ss [grow]\&
How much more memory each grant request asks for.
Optional; defaults to
.Cm exponential .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm exponential
Double the step for each throttle that follows soon after a grow.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm step No = Ar size
The first request, and the unit later ones double.
Default
.Cm 512MiB .
.It Cm escalate_within No = Ar duration
How soon after a grow a throttle still doubles the step.
Default
.Cm 10s .
.It Cm cap No = Ar count
The most steps one request asks for.
Default
.Cm 64 .
.El
.El
.Ss [release]\&
When the guest returns memory to the host, and how much.
Optional; defaults to
.Cm titrate .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm titrate
Release a fixed step at a time.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm step No = Ar size
How much one release returns.
Default
.Cm 256MiB .
.It Cm after No = Ar count
Consecutive ticks the guest must have
.Cm step
to spare before a release.
Default
.Cm 3 .
.It Cm cooldown No = Ar duration
Minimum time after a resize before a release.
May be 0.
Default
.Cm 30s .
.El
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm sweep
Release all spare memory at once, once it has held for
.Cm hold .
A throttle, a breach, or less than
.Cm min
to spare starts the hold over.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm min No = Ar size
The least spare memory that counts towards the hold.
Default
.Cm 256MiB .
.It Cm hold No = Ar duration
How long the spare must hold before a release.
May be 0.
Default
.Cm 5m .
.It Cm cooldown No = Ar duration
Minimum time after a resize before a release.
May be 0.
Default
.Cm 30s .
.El
.El
.Ss [exhaustion]\&
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm recover_after No = Ar count
Consecutive calm ticks that end an exhaustion.
A tick is calm when the workload neither throttles nor breaches, and the guest
has a memory block to spare.
Default
.Cm 3 .
.El
.Ss [exhaustion.mode]\&
What the agent does when the guest reaches its ceiling.
Optional; defaults to
.Cm stall
with a
.Cm 60s
timeout.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm stall
Keep the brake on until
.Cm timeout ,
then release it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm timeout No = Ar duration
How long to keep the brake on before releasing it and letting the workload
reach
.Va memory.max .
Default
.Cm 60s .
.El
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm kill
Release the brake immediately, and have the kernel kill the whole cgroup when
it reaches
.Va memory.max .
.El
.Ss [preflight]\&
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm thp_always No = Qq Cm fail | Qq Cm warn
What preflight does when
.Va transparent_hugepage=always :
fail, or only warn.
Default
.Cm fail .
.El
.Ss [metrics]\&
Optional.
Without it, the agent serves no metrics.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm listen No = Ar address
Address to serve OpenMetrics on, for example
.Ql 127.0.0.1:9651 .
Required.
.El
.Sh SIZING
.Ss service_reserve
With the workload stopped, read
.Va memory.current
of
.Pa system.slice
and anything else outside the workload cgroup, and add a margin.
Too little lets a throttled workload squeeze the agent itself; too much wastes
granted memory.
.Ss burst_reserve
The reserve must meet two conditions.
.Pp
First, it must hold what the workload allocates during one grow round trip:
the round trip on your host multiplied by the workload's unthrottled allocation
rate.
At 1GiB/s and 300ms, that is 300MiB.
It must also hold the workload's largest single allocation, since the kernel
throttles after an allocation, not during it.
.Pp
Second, it must be wider than the point at which the kernel's throttle stops the
workload altogether.
The throttle delay grows with the overshoot past
.Va memory.high
and saturates at about two seconds per allocation.
A reserve wider than that point holds a refused workload indefinitely; a
narrower one only slows it on its way to
.Va memory.max .
To find the point, lower
.Cm burst_reserve
until a workload that is refused memory starts reaching
.Va memory.max ,
visible as
.Va pazari_agent_max_events
increasing, and use several times that value.
.Pp
Measure again after changing the transparent hugepage mode, adding or removing
swap, or changing how the workload allocates.
.Ss Reference measurements
Taken with
.Xr pazari-stress 1
in a guest without swap, faulting anonymous memory one page at a time as fast
as the kernel allowed.
Measure on your own hardware.
.Pp
Grow round trip, from request to
.Va MemTotal
rising, over 11 grows:
.Bl -column "tick.interval" "median" "95th percentile" -offset indent
.It Sy tick.interval Ta Sy median Ta Sy 95th percentile
.It 500ms Ta 302ms Ta 402ms
.It 100ms Ta 118ms Ta 180ms
.El
.Pp
Time for a refused workload to reach
.Va memory.max ,
over two runs of 360 seconds:
.Bl -column "burst_reserve" "never; stopped 14\-18MiB into the reserve" -offset indent
.It Sy burst_reserve Ta Sy result
.It none Ta under 5s
.It 16MiB Ta 11s and 35s
.It 64MiB Ta never; stopped 17\-18MiB into the reserve
.It 256MiB Ta never; stopped 14\-15MiB into the reserve
.El
.Ss Usage, not commit
Size reserves from
.Va memory.current ,
not
.Va Committed_AS .
Mapped but untouched memory counts towards commit but not usage, and the agent
sees only usage.
.Sh METRICS
With
.Cm [metrics]
configured, the agent publishes the following, each prefixed
.Ql pazari_agent_ .
.Ss Gauges
.Bl -tag -width "workload_usage_bytes" -compact
.It Va mode
1 for the current mode, 0 for the others, labelled
.Va mode .
.It Va memory_high_bytes
.Va memory.high
as last written.
.It Va memory_max_bytes
.Va memory.max
as last written.
.It Va brake_released
1 while
.Va memory.high
equals
.Va memory.max .
.It Va total_mem_bytes
The guest's
.Va MemTotal .
.It Va ceiling_bytes
The ceiling set by the host.
Absent until the host has set one.
.It Va workload_usage_bytes
.Va memory.current
of the workload cgroup.
.It Va swap_used_bytes
Swap used by the workload cgroup.
.It Va high_events
The cgroup's
.Va high
event count.
.It Va max_events
The cgroup's
.Va max
event count.
.It Va psi_some10
The workload's memory pressure.
.It Va connected
1 while connected to the host.
.El
.Ss Counters
.Bl -tag -width "throttle_reclaim_shortfalls_total" -compact
.It Va throttle_wakes_total
Times the agent was woken by a throttle.
.It Va grant_requests_total
Grant requests sent.
.It Va grants_total
Grants received.
.It Va denies_total
Refusals received, labelled
.Va reason .
.It Va offers_total
Offers to release sent.
.It Va reclaims_total
Reclaims started on the workload cgroup.
.It Va reclaim_asked_bytes_total
Bytes those reclaims asked the kernel for.
.It Va exhaustions_total
Times the agent became exhausted.
.It Va throttle_reclaims_total
Throttles answered by reclaiming.
.It Va throttle_reclaim_shortfalls_total
Throttle reclaims that fell short.
.It Va connections_total
Connections established.
.It Va disconnections_total
Connections lost.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/pazari/agent.toml
Default configuration file.
.It Pa share/doc/pazari/examples/agent.toml
Annotated example, installed with the package.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A guest that boots with 2GiB, keeps 512MiB for its own services, uses a 256MiB
burst reserve, and stalls for up to five minutes when exhausted:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[tick]
interval = "500ms"

[workload]
cgroup = "/sys/fs/cgroup/workload.slice"
service_reserve = "512MiB"
burst_reserve = "256MiB"

[workload.backend]
kind = "systemd"
unit = "workload.slice"

[host.transport]
kind = "vsock"

[exhaustion.mode]
kind = "stall"
timeout = "300s"

[metrics]
listen = "127.0.0.1:9651"
.Ed
